  "arrangerNotes": "6/8 time (eighth = 0.5 beat). Verified against the LilyPond score on Hungarian Wikipedia (Silcher's tune; the score's key signature says A minor but the melody is in C major). The score's rests between phrases are kept. Simplification: the chromatic F♯ in 'und ruhig fließt der Rhein' (F♯–G) is played as 4 (F), since tongue drums have no chromatic notes. D drum: as written (range 1 to high 3), D minLayout 13. C drum: the C drum has no high 2/3, so the last phrase 'der Gipfel des Berges funkelt im Abendsonnenschein' (score events 55–71) is played one octave lower; C minLayout 11. C and D arrangements differ where noted above (each fits its own drum).",
  "verified": true
}
